{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPMk4Evjkw7yMNJct6BP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The data don't support the hypothesis that more diverse suppliers raise export growth. The raw association is positive, but it disappears once I control for firm characteristics measured in 2020.\n\n- **Preferred estimate:** a one-standard-deviation increase in supplier diversity is associated with 0.05 more points of export growth. The standard error is 0.25 and p = 0.84. The 95% confidence interval is about −0.43 to +0.54, so effects larger than about half a point are unlikely.\n- **Why it changes:** the bivariate slope is 1.78 (p < 1e-11). Adjusting for firm size, years exporting and prior export growth shrinks it to roughly zero. This fits larger, more established firms having both more suppliers and faster growth.\n- **Specification:** the preferred model is a linear regression on all the 2020 firm characteristics plus region and product-group effects, with robust standard errors, on 2,000 firms.\n- **Excluded variable:** I left out `buyer_rating_2023` because it is measured after the supplier data and is plausibly an outcome of diversity. Adding it flips the estimate to −2.41, which isn't a causal effect.\n- **Specifications:** I ran six in total, and all are listed in the report, including the ones I didn't prefer.\n- **Caveat:** this is a single cross-section, so unobserved confounders could still bias the estimate.\n\nI recorded the conclusion as \"no effect\".\n\nFiles are in the working folder:\n- report.md\n- final_answer.json"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1613,"cache_read_input_tokens":10694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1613,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":494,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"122d7b97-10d6-4922-957c-7e652a69db31","uuid":"2ae45e49-b6da-486b-9a71-6e6509367377"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":29385,"duration_api_ms":31394,"num_turns":8,"result":"The data don't support the hypothesis that more diverse suppliers raise export growth. The raw association is positive, but it disappears once I control for firm characteristics measured in 2020.\n\n- **Preferred estimate:** a one-standard-deviation increase in supplier diversity is associated with 0.05 more points of export growth. The standard error is 0.25 and p = 0.84. The 95% confidence interval is about −0.43 to +0.54, so effects larger than about half a point are unlikely.\n- **Why it changes:** the bivariate slope is 1.78 (p < 1e-11). Adjusting for firm size, years exporting and prior export growth shrinks it to roughly zero. This fits larger, more established firms having both more suppliers and faster growth.\n- **Specification:** the preferred model is a linear regression on all the 2020 firm characteristics plus region and product-group effects, with robust standard errors, on 2,000 firms.\n- **Excluded variable:** I left out `buyer_rating_2023` because it is measured after the supplier data and is plausibly an outcome of diversity. Adding it flips the estimate to −2.41, which isn't a causal effect.\n- **Specifications:** I ran six in total, and all are listed in the report, including the ones I didn't prefer.\n- **Caveat:** this is a single cross-section, so unobserved confounders could still bias the estimate.\n\nI recorded the conclusion as \"no effect\".\n\nFiles are in the working folder:\n- report.md\n- final_answer.json","session_id":"122d7b97-10d6-4922-957c-7e652a69db31","total_cost_usd":0.08692454999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5953,"cache_read_input_tokens":48296,"output_tokens":2748,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5953}},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":